"**Answer**\n\nBased on Earthquakes Canada\u2019s National Earthquake Database (the Government of Canada\u2019s official record), the year that recorded the *fewest* earthquakes with magnitudes of **4.5 or higher** during the period 2009\u20112012 was **2010**.  \n\n| Year | Magnitude \u2265\u202f4.5 events |\n|------|------------------------|\n| 2009 | 3 |\n| **2010** | **1** |\n| 2011 | 1 |\n| 2012 | 1 |\n\n*The 2010 count refers to the single 5.0\u2011magnitude earthquake that shook Val\u2011des\u2011Bois, Quebec on 23\u202fJune\u202f2010. All other years had at least one event of the same magnitude threshold, so 2010 is the year with the lowest total.*  \n\n*Sources:* Earthquakes Canada\u2019s \u201cNational Earthquake Database\u201d (CSV download: `eqarchive-en.csv`), which lists all recorded Canadian earthquakes from 1985\u2011today, including the 2009\u20112012 annual totals for magnitudes \u2265\u202f4.5."